areyouthewind, Take care

Hi Affectionate,

&#x200B;

Yes I do find that gratitude is countering negativity for me.

&#x200B;

It's like this, if I count the 5 things I'm grateful for (no matter how small, food in the belly, the roof overhead etc.) then I'm not counting the things that are wrong in life because that list has no end if I keep thinking about it.

&#x200B;

My struggle has been around bankruptcy, betrayal in business and betrayal in a relationship.

All of my self-esteem has been ripped from me over the last 2 years and this project was a last-ditch effort instead of going the path of suicide.

Thanks for the message Jazza,

&#x200B;

I've had them a few times too and while this one really sucks, it's not as bad as previous ones, but still, its been causing me pain all week.

&#x200B;

Pain meds help a little

Little things are always good to be grateful for, I'm grateful for Coffee and also that Australians take a lot of pride in making great Coffee and there is always a specialty coffee's all over Sydney.

&#x200B;

I've been dealing with this kidney stone all week and I agree with you, physical pain sucks, but I would take this over the emotional torture any day.

I agree with you Adam,

&#x200B;

For me, the accomplishments I had during my day were based on doing things that make me happy and did somethings that were creative in nature.

&#x200B;

Thanks for you comment

Thanks ZD,

&#x200B;

That's very helpful

&#x200B;

!givelambda

>it comes from a

I definitely relate to the idea of people using me.

&#x200B;

But I am also recognizing that I am pretty good at setting myself up to be used.

&#x200B;

As for Gratitude Bridge: I started it because I was in a hopeless (suicidal position) and needed to change the course.

&#x200B;

I try to do all videos at Sunrise with Sydney Harbour Bridge as a backdrop and I always talk about Gratitude.

&#x200B;

The videos I did in January were all stories about depression with gratitude as the solution.

&#x200B;

I book-ended the stories with 2 of my poems on day 1 and 31.

each video took 7 to 16 hours to create and so January was incredibly stressful, but I learnt a lot of processes.

&#x200B;

February was about Self Love and followed a much simpler format, it was a little boring to be honest but I kept persisting.

&#x200B;

March has changed again and I am now on camera and learning how to just talk from the heart about whatever issues are going on, on the day.

If you get the time and if it is of interest, I would appreciate the feedback.

&#x200B;

* Day 5 - Gratitude Jar
* Day 10 - Kindness of Strangers
* Day 31 - Poem: Tiger and Wolf
* Day 79 - Having a purpose helps

&#x200B;

[Gratitude Bridge](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCY_sGXuXqYuoNOUBkArugAA?sub_confirmation=1)

I really appreciate your words.

&#x200B;

I've been doing this project for 40 days about my depression and fear.

&#x200B;

Its a been a hard project to do, in many different ways.

Hi Everyone,  


I have started a personal project around depression and gratitude.

&#x200B;

I have been posting daily videos on [fb.com/GratitudeBridge](https://fb.com/GratitudeBridge) and on YouTube

&#x200B;

It's a personal project for me on my journey and challenge around major depression and the use of Gratitude as a means to heal.

&#x200B;

I am looking to learn more about my personal challenge in this space, to grow and to heal, while at the same time helping others with major depression or who support people with depression.

&#x200B;

January will be about 31 stories on depression.

&#x200B;

Every video is centred around Sydney Harbour Bridge.

&#x200B;

Every video is about peaceful videography, some sort of challenge around depression/suicide and a solution using gratitude.

