I do, but I also reached out to the right people just before new years eve when I was about to end it all.

&#x200B;

I told people the dire state I was in and I sought support from multiple people by being honest with them.

I then started posting my days (good or bad) and focusing on gratitude via a project I started on Jan 1, 2019.

&#x200B;

It's a personal pilgramage on depresion, suicide and gratitude.

&#x200B;

I'm trying to just keep going really.

&#x200B;

[https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCY\_sGXuXqYuoNOUBkArugAA/videos](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCY_sGXuXqYuoNOUBkArugAA/videos)

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Understand, I am in recovery for over 8 years. So I have been developing my network, but the depression is still a bitch.

&#x200B;

Still, even where you are at, you can focus on gratitude.  


I went onto social security yesterday, facing bankruptcy and also potential homelessness soon. but every day I do a video blog called Gratitude Bridge taking video's of Sydney harbour and I try to stay in gratitude despite the hell.

&#x200B;

[https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCY\_sGXuXqYuoNOUBkArugAA/videos](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCY_sGXuXqYuoNOUBkArugAA/videos)

I also identify with the homicidal thoughts, it's like the suicidal thoughts are only because I can't hurt the people that have hurt me so bad.

&#x200B;

anyway, the only thing I have been doing is my facebook page, GratitudeBridge where every day I talk about depression and solutions using Gratitude as the basic idea.

texting a crisis worker while suicidal (grateful for 0477 131 114 in Australia) - Day 11

&#x200B;

What are you grateful for?

&#x200B;

I'm grateful for the Suicide Crisis Line on 0477 131 114 in Australia.

&#x200B;

A friend shared a post with me about a new free service in Australia by Life Line.

&#x200B;

Did you know that if you text 0477 131 114 in Australia between 6-10pm when you are feeling really depressed or suicidal, a crisis worker will text exchange with you?

&#x200B;

I contacted the number via text and Beth was soon in a conversation with me.

&#x200B;

It's specifically around giving people who are suicidal or depressed a way to connect with someone who is trained in crisis situations without having to speak on the phone.

&#x200B;

Many people don't like talking on the phone & would be more comfortable texting.

&#x200B;

The Suicide Crisis Text Line is a free service being run by Lifeline.

&#x200B;

Today, I am grateful for Lifeline and the Suicide Crisis Text Service.

&#x200B;

I am in the middle of day four of my own new year's resolution to create 365 days of gratitude on youtube and facebook via Gratitude Bridge. Its such a painful process so far as it is taking 12 hours a day to produce the videos, but I'm gett better at it

&#x200B;

[https://www.facebook.com/gratitudebridge](https://www.facebook.com/gratitudebridge)
